      "claim": "The `covers.set` label on the first acceptance criterion, \"the two states a kept adopt leaves with a `pr_url`,\" reads as if it names the complete set of such states, but it is not exhaustive: `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` is a third state `_adopt` can also keep with a `pr_url` (through the same non-`STALE_PUSH_STATES` branch at `cli.py:3313-3315`), and it is also outside `_PACKAGED`, so it hits the identical fabrication bug this spec fixes for `ORPHANED`/`REBUTTAL_UNJUDGED`. The spec's own Problem and Out-of-scope sections correctly disambiguate this (\"the two states a kept adopt can now leave\" / \"reachable before `SA-0429` too\"), so the omission is deliberate and disclosed, not an error — but the `covers.set` wording itself, read in isolation, overclaims completeness. This is cosmetic and does not affect what the cell would build.",
